config HWINFO_TELINK_B87
	bool "Telink TLSR8278 hwinfo driver"
	default y
	depends on DT_HAS_TELINK_B87_HWINFO_ENABLED
	select HWINFO_HAS_DRIVER
	select SOC_TLSR8278_MSPI
	help
	  The device ID is the 128-bit unique ID of the internal flash, read
	  with the flash's command 0x4b from SRAM with interrupts locked. The
	  reset cause is taken at boot: RESET_WATCHDOG when the watchdog's
	  reset status bit (0x72 bit 0) is set, RESET_LOW_POWER_WAKE when a
	  wakeup status bit of analog register 0x44 is (a wake from deep
	  sleep), RESET_POR when neither is. A reset by software (0x6f bit 5)
	  or by the RESETB pin sets no flag the chip documents, so it reads as
	  RESET_POR as well. hwinfo_clear_reset_cause() clears both flags and
	  the cause taken at boot.
